// std/xml is in the specification's package list (§13.4) and in no release
// yet. The refusal must land HERE, at the `use`, and not in the backend: a
// program that passes `check` and then fails `build` is the one inconsistency
// the `check` verb exists to prevent.
//
// This fixture named std/regex until regex shipped, and std/http until http
// shipped — each time it went green by accident, because the package it was
// testing had become real. If xml ever ships, move this to another name from
// std_planned() rather than deleting it; the behaviour it pins is the
// `use`-site refusal, not the particular package.
use "std/xml"

func main() {
    say xml.decode("<a/>")
}
